ction regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate ~18%. Rolling back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-errors-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 453694, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CEF9C1Ga9TERCukPwYyjMo", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-errors-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 453694, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CEF9C1Ga9TERCukPwYyjMo", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 459307, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. Error rates are back to normal.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The service is called `payments-api`, not \"payments\", so I used that name.\n- This morning's release, v5.1.0, was degraded in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%.\n- v5.0.0 was its most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it in all three regions.\n- After the rollback, the service reports healthy and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, payments-api), and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n- My first attempt timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key so it couldn't page twice. Only one incident exists.\n- Its summary was written while the rollback was running, so it says \"rolling back\" rather than \"rolled back.\"\n\n**Still to do:** v5.1.0 needs a look to find what caused the errors before anyone redeploys it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu