8}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019EuHxi2a9KN8zbeWnuBdk4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-api errors after v5.1.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "payments-api v5.1.0 (deployed this morning) is degraded in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate ~18%. Rolling back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-errors-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FNZwfKo7bvmWwS2NqDd4cN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ML2vvU13eNCE8zgMs5u6TZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "No incident was created; retrying with the same idempotency key so it can't double-page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CEF9C1Ga9TERCukPwYyjMo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-api errors after v5.1.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "payments-api v5.1.0 (deployed this morning) is degraded in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate ~18%. Rolling back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-errors-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. Error rates are back to normal.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The service is called `payments-api`, not \"payments\", so I used that name.\n- This morning's release, v5.1.0, was degraded in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%.\n- v5.0.0 was its most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it in all three regions.\n- After the rollback, the service reports healthy and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, payments-api), and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n- My first attempt timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key so it couldn't page twice. Only one incident exists.\n- Its summary was written while the rollback was running, so it says \"rolling back\" rather than \"rolled back.\"\n\n**Still to do:** v5.1.0 needs a look to find what caused the errors before anyone redeploys it.", "type": "text"}]}]}